## ASSEMBLED SECTION



### <img src="https://flagcdn.com/tr.svg" width="32" alt="Turkey" style={{display: 'inline', verticalAlign: 'middle', position: 'relative', top: '-2px', marginRight: '8px', border: '1px solid #d1d5db', borderRadius: '2px'}} />Turkey

Turkey escalates authoritarian consolidation through unprecedented judicial weaponization while maintaining strategic autonomy across multiple domains. Erdoğan's appointment of hardline prosecutor Akın Gürlek as Justice Minister - who sought 2,000+ years for imprisoned opposition leader İmamoğlu - represents the most aggressive institutionalization of judicial persecution since the republic's founding, triggering parliamentary brawls and international condemnation. The regime simultaneously fragments opposition through systematic mayor defection campaigns while continuing the transactional Kurdish peace process linked to constitutional amendment arithmetic for extending presidential rule beyond 2028. Externally, Turkey maintains its regional broker positioning through routine NATO ally engagement despite minor friction over counterterrorism policy, while Foreign Minister Fidan's calculated silence on nuclear weapons acquisition signals potential strategic ambiguity regarding deterrence capabilities. The economic stabilization program continues under orthodox Central Bank management despite upward inflation pressure, with international promotion of Turkish resilience proceeding through established channels.

**Key developments:**

- **Domestic:** Erdoğan appointed Istanbul chief prosecutor Akın Gürlek as Justice Minister, who demanded over 2,000 years imprisonment for İmamoğlu and oversaw unprecedented crackdown on CHP. Opposition MPs physically confronted Gürlek during oath ceremony, with CHP calling the appointment 'an attack on the rule of law.'
- **Domestic:** From Silivri prison, İmamoğlu told Reuters that Erdoğan should call elections 'now' and predicted Erdoğan would lose if he ran again. İmamoğlu maintains 18-hour working days while facing over 10 cases, with the main corruption trial beginning next month seeking 2,000+ years imprisonment.
- **Domestic:** Keçiören mayor Mesut Özarslan resigned from CHP citing systematic harassment and threats from party leadership, with reports of multiple other CHP mayors preparing defections. AKP kulislerinde claims 3-4 additional Ankara mayors may defect, potentially shifting municipal council majorities.
- **Diplomatic:** President Erdoğan met with Greek PM Mitsotakis to discuss Aegean and Eastern Mediterranean issues, Gaza peace process, and Syria stabilization. Both leaders emphasized maintaining dialogue channels and cooperation on regional security challenges.
- **Diplomatic:** Foreign Minister Fidan's televised comments about PKK presence in Iraq and need for Iraqi government action prompted Baghdad to summon Turkey's ambassador. Turkey's foreign ministry clarified the statements addressed PKK terrorist threat to Iraq's territorial integrity.

<Accordion title="Other Stories">
- **MHP celebrates 57th anniversary with Bahçeli's 'Terror-free Turkey' message** — MHP leader Devlet Bahçeli marked his party's 57th anniversary with speeches emphasizing the 'Terror-free Turkey' process and brotherhood between Turks and Kurds. Erdoğan sent a 57-rose bouquet with Turkish flag motifs to congratulate Bahçeli. *([hurriyet.com.tr](https://www.hurriyet.com.tr/gundem/mhp-lideri-bahceli-kardes-kavgasini-onlemeye-kararliyiz-mhp-gereken-bedelleri-odemeye-hazir-43103889))*
- **Bahçeli praises Turkish TV drama, calls actor to offer gift** — MHP leader Devlet Bahçeli called the lead actor of the 'Yeraltı' (Underground) TV series to praise the show for encouraging youth to avoid bad habits. He offered to send a 'bozkurt' (grey wolf) painting as a gift to the cast. *([sozcu.com.tr](https://sozcu.com.tr/bahceli-izledigi-bu-diziye-hayran-kaldi-hemen-basrol-oyuncusunu-aradi-p294208))*
- **Foreign Minister Fidan refuses to answer nuclear weapons question during TV interview** — During a CNN Türk interview, Foreign Minister Hakan Fidan remained silent when asked whether Turkey should acquire nuclear weapons. His non-response to the nuclear question drew attention from Israeli and Greek media and sparked social media discussion. *([sozcu.com.tr](https://sozcu.com.tr/hakan-fidan-in-cevap-veremedigi-soru-canli-yayinda-dondu-kaldi-p292623))*
- **Central Bank raises 2026 inflation forecast amid economic pressures** — TCMB Governor Fatih Karahan announced upward revision of 2026 year-end inflation forecasts during the quarterly inflation report. The bank maintained its cautious and data-dependent monetary policy approach while reserves showed decline due to gold price effects. *([tacirler.com.tr](https://tacirler.com.tr/tcmb-2026-1-ceyrek-enflasyon-raporu--3862))*
- **DEM Party delegation prepares for İmralı visit as part of 'Terror-free Turkey' process** — DEM Party announced that its İmralı delegation would visit Abdullah Öcalan on February 16. This follows meetings between DEM Party leaders and President Erdoğan as part of the ongoing 'Terror-free Turkey' initiative. *([dailysabah.com](https://dailysabah.com/politics/war-on-terror/erdogan-terms-terror-free-turkiye-a-success-as-key-report-awaited))*
- **Bloomberg reports speculation about Bilal Erdoğan as potential successor** — US-based Bloomberg published analysis suggesting President Erdoğan's son Bilal Erdoğan is being politically groomed as a potential successor. The report discussed his increasing profile and possible roles within AKP leadership structure. *([bloomberg.com](https://bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-02-10/who-will-succeed-erdogan-son-bilal-s-rising-profile-fuels-talk-in-turkey))*
- **MİT chief Kalın meets with Libyan Prime Minister in Tripoli** — National Intelligence Organization head İbrahim Kalın met with Libyan PM Abdulhamid Dibeybe in Tripoli to discuss regional issues and coordinated international efforts to support Libya's political process. *([ahaber.com.tr](https://www.ahaber.com.tr/dunya/2026/02/12/mit-baskani-kalin-libya-basbakani-ile-bir-araya-geldi))*
- **Turkish Armed Forces participate in NATO's Steadfast Dart 2026 exercise** — Turkish military participated in NATO's largest exercise with TCG Anadolu and TB-3 drones making notable impression. NATO praised Turkish forces' capabilities during the multinational training in Germany. *([hurriyet.com.tr](https://www.hurriyet.com.tr/dunya/natodan-turk-askerleri-paylasimi-gucluyuz-cesuruz-haziriz-43108738))*
- **Erdoğan issues gambling warning, leading public banks to restrict betting payments** — President Erdoğan warned that gambling addiction threatens family institutions, saying 'every phone has become a casino.' Following his statement, three state banks restricted payments to gambling websites through mobile banking. *([haberler.com](https://www.haberler.com/ekonomi/erdogan-uyardi-3-kamu-bankasi-sans-oyunlarina-19549393-haberi/))*
- **Fidan's Iraq PKK comments draw diplomatic protest from Baghdad** — Foreign Minister Hakan Fidan's statements about PKK's presence in Iraq and the need for Iraqi government action prompted Baghdad to summon Turkey's ambassador. Turkey's foreign ministry clarified that statements were misrepresented. *([bursahakimiyet.com.tr](https://bursahakimiyet.com.tr/gundem/hakan-fidan-in-sincar-sozleri-sonrasi-irak-buyukelciyi-cagirdi-disisleri-bakanligi-harekete-gecti-1575543))*
